-5d1b-9036-7aa4df8f20af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571409 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571290 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571409 #edb/ref 1069 "q-23926" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571409 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571409 #edb/ref 1071 "The surface area of a cube is $150$ square units. Find the length of the edges of the cube." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571409 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "661ca87c-9ae5-589f-ace6-f92ef07fb654" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571409 #edb/ref 1074 "The surface area $S$ of a cube is made up of $6$ congruent squares. So, the area $A$ of one face is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{S}{6}=\\frac{150}{6}=25\\,.\n$$\n\nSince $A={s}^{2},$ where $s$ is the length of an edge, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt{A}=\\sqrt{25}=5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the edges is $5$ units." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571415 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571415 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107323" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571415 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571415 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the surface area of the cube whose sides each have length $4\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{in}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571415 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "77a60330-8cf9-5eed-a2b7-ae915d42d5e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571415 #edb/ref 1074 "The surface area $S$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nS=6{s}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting $s=4\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{in}$ into the formula, we get \n\n$$\nS=6(4\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{in})^{2}=672\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571422 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571325 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571422 #edb/ref 1069 "q-118510" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571422 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571422 #edb/ref 1071 "The lateral surface area of a cube is $400\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.$ Find the length of the edges of the cube." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571422 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "84fa227b-da46-520b-a245-2527cb980b2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571422 #edb/ref 1074 "The lateral surface area ${S}_{L}$ of a cube is made up of $4$ congruent squares. So, the area $A$ of one face is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{{S}_{L}}{4}=\\frac{400}{4}=100\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}\\,.\n$$\n\nSince $A={s}^{2},$ where $s$ is the length of an edge, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt{A}=\\sqrt{100}=10\\,\\text{ft}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the edges is $10\\,\\text{ft}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571429 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571293 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571429 #edb/ref 1069 "q-86336" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571429 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571429 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/5e/5eef04daa0a8ac1a590b3a0da378d9184ad9b82c5e4834c5079ccb4f3665cced.png)\n\nDetermine the surface area for the cube above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571429 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "98cd99a4-4813-5a81-8e79-78ee88e169c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571429 #edb/ref 1074 "The surface area $S$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nS=6{s}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting $s=2\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm}$ into the formula, we get \n\n$$\nS=6(2\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm})^{2}=120\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571449 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571292 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571449 #edb/ref 1069 "q-86353" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571449 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571449 #edb/ref 1071 "The surface area of a cube is $294\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.$ Find the length of the edges of the cube." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571449 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f1ef2b0d-aa7e-55cc-9472-24fb79eacf8f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571449 #edb/ref 1074 "The surface area $S$ of a cube is made up of $6$ congruent squares. So, the area $A$ of one face is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{S}{6}=\\frac{294}{6}=49\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}\\,.\n$$\n\nSince $A={s}^{2},$ where $s$ is the length of an edge, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt{A}=\\sqrt{49}=7\\,\\text{cm}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the edges is $7\\,\\text{cm}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571453 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571294 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571453 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107341" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571453 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571453 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/4a/4ab1cb82bca3650868b7e654cb52d3eb7a0c3101ab4d6a3458485865ae353264.png)\n\nDetermine the lateral surface area for the cube above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571453 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fa36ef42-622c-5ec4-b237-5aa6a8f72c36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571453 #edb/ref 1074 "The lateral surface area ${S}_{L}$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}=4{s}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting $s=3\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm}$ into the formula, we get \n\n$$\n{S}_{L}=4(3\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm})^{2}=180\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
